ster that TestKubeRegistrationClusterSetup forms, so it only runs as part of TestKubeRegistrationSuite\n\nClaude's conclusion:\nThis confirms the same \"500 user name not set\" broker error already documented in live-investigation.md caused `TestKubeRegistrationClusterSetup` to fail in this run, which cascaded directly into this `TestKubeRegistrationAddNode` failure.\n\nLikely root cause: `TestKubeRegistrationAddNode` failed purely as a downstream consequence of `TestKubeRegistrationClusterSetup` failing earlier in this same suite run — `requireKubeRegCluster` (helpers_test.go:151, called from addnode_test.go:80) panics because no cluster was ever formed, exactly matching the reported \"No cluster was set up\" message. The root cause is the one already recorded in `live-investigation.md` for this run: the Proxmox broker rejected VM creation for `edge-dev2` with `500 user name not set` while concurrently provisioning the 4 cluster devices — a broker-side auth/session error, not a pillar/EVE bug. Harness teardown already ran (devices and SDN torn down), so there's no further live EVE state to inspect for this specific failure. Per `live-ledger.md`, this exact `\"500 user name not set\"` signature is a known, recurring (if infrequent) broker flake first seen 2026-11-09 (run #12, `TestNodeClusterSuite/TestMgmtProxy`), part of a broader recurring class of Proxmox-broker VM-provisioning flakes. This failure shares its root cause with the earlier `TestKubeRegistrationClusterSetup` failure in this same run.","time":{"start":1795387657000,"stop":1795387865230,"duration":208230}},{"uid":"cdb053e7daf72371","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/36/#testresult/cdb053e7daf72371","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795307461000,"stop":1795307654190,"duration":193190}},{"uid":"39ca9ec4dd61ec6f","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/31/#testresult/39ca9ec4dd61ec6f","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795213040000,"stop":1795213227760,"durati